Test Case-1
Design a circular waveguide for the TEII mode to transmit a signal at 10 GHz. The material is air, and the waveguide length is 2 meters.

Determine the minimum radius of the waveguide.
Calculate the cutoff wavelength, guide wavelength, and characteristic impedance.
AIM:
To determine the propagation characteristics of circular waveguide in terms of Cutoff wavelength. Guidewavelength and characteristic impedance.
CODE:
// Constants
c = 3e8;
f = 10e9;
p = 1.841;
er = 1;
mu_r = 1;
eta = 377 / sqrt(er);
// Calculations
lambda = c / f;
// Minimum radius
r_min = (p * c) / (2 * %pi * f * sqrt(er));
// Design radius (10% margin)
r = 1.1 * r_min;
// Cutoff wavelength
lambda_c = (2 * %pi * r) / p;
// Propagation constant
k = (2 * %pi * f * sqrt(er)) / c;
kc = p / r;
beta = sqrt(k^2 - kc^2);
// Guide wavelength
lambda_g = (2 * %pi) / beta;
// TE wave impedance
Z = eta * k / beta;
disp("Minimum Radius (m): " + string(r_min));
disp("Design Radius (m): " + string(r));
disp("Cutoff Wavelength (m): " + string(lambda_c));
disp("Guide Wavelength (m): " + string(lambda_g));
disp("Characteristic Impedance (Ohms): " + string(Z));

